course: dictionary
lesson: 3168
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives three meanings for emperor, so context tells you which one is right. «In 221 BC the king of Qin conquered all the warring kingdoms and called himself the First Emperor.» The clues are conquered and kingdoms, so emperor means a ruler of many lands.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Male emperor penguins huddle in thousands, each with an egg on his feet.» The clues are penguins, huddle and egg, so emperor here is a kind of penguin, not a ruler.
explain: Ask what the text is about. A history text talks about rulers, kingdoms and dynasties. A nature text talks about animals, ice and eggs. Put each meaning into the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: An emperor is a man who rules an empire, a group of many countries or lands.
fact: «Caesar Augustus was the Roman emperor when Jesus was born.»
fact: The emperor penguin is the biggest kind of penguin.
fact: «The Kangxi Emperor ruled 61 years, 1661–1722, the longest reign in Chinese history.»
fact: Emperor penguin fathers keep the egg on their feet for about two months, and they eat nothing while they wait.
exercise: «In 221 BC the king of Qin conquered all the warring kingdoms and called himself the First Emperor.» What is an emperor in this sentence? | A penguin that lives on ice | *A ruler who rules many lands | A kind of cold weather | A small village chief
exercise: «Male emperor penguins huddle in thousands, each with an egg on his feet.» What is an emperor in this sentence? | *A penguin | A Roman soldier | A king of a small village | A ship on the sea
exercise: The sentence «The emperor penguin is the biggest kind of penguin.» tells you about the word emperor. What does it show? | It is a story about a vain king | *It is a kind of penguin, not a ruler | It is a ruler of many lands | It is a Roman title
test: «The Kangxi Emperor ruled 61 years, the longest reign in Chinese history.» What does emperor mean here? | A school subject about the weather | A penguin with a warm belly | *A man who rules an empire
test: Mia reads «each with an egg on his feet» and says emperor must mean a king. What should she check first? | Whether the word has the right number of letters | *Whether the clues, like egg and feet, point to a penguin | Whether king and emperor always mean the same thing
exam: Which meaning of emperor fits «The Emperor's New Clothes is a story about a vain ruler who is fooled»? | A kind of cold weather | A small bird that cannot fly | A school subject about the sea | *A man who rules an empire
